    <medicalInfoContent>
      <Value Culture="en-us"><![CDATA[]]></Value>
      <Value Culture="nl-nl"><![CDATA[[
  {
    "backgroundColor": "",
    "backgroundImage": "[]",
    "backgroundImageOverlap": "0",
    "contentItemContentText": "{\r\n  \"markup\": \"<p>How the cast is applied depends on the fracture or injury to your arm or leg. There are two methods:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Around your entire arm or leg. This is called a full cast.</li>\\n<li>Only on the underside of your arm or leg. This is called a splint.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>The doctor will determine which cast you will receive.<br>There are two types of cast. The type of cast you receive depends on the fracture and the injury:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>After an accident or surgery, you will usually receive a plaster cast first.</li>\\n<li>Once your arm or leg is no longer swollen, you will usually receive a plastic cast. You may also receive a plastic cast after the removal of stitches</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>If you break your arm, you may need to rest it in a sling.<br>A sling is a strap with a loop that hangs around your neck. Your arm hangs in the loop.</p>\",\r\n  \"blocks\": {\r\n    \"contentData\": [],\r\n    \"settingsData\": []\r\n  }\r\n}",
    "contentItemTitle": "About the treatment",
    "key": "c79eeba8-8c7a-446f-b6bf-7a01c7bba7b4",
    "name": "About the treatment",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "hoofdContentBlokken",
    "PropType": null
  }
]]]></Value>
    </medicalInfoContent>
    <medicalInfoContentBL>
      <Value Culture="en-us"><![CDATA[]]></Value>
      <Value Culture="nl-nl"><![CDATA[{
  "layout": {
    "Umbraco.BlockList": [
      {
        "contentUdi": "umb://element/d3669840fd834cbfbe19d0c18ec3b6d2"
      }
    ]
  },
  "contentData": [
    {
      "backgroundImage": [],
      "backgroundImageOverlap": "0",
      "contentItemContentText": {
        "markup": "<p>How the cast is applied depends on the fracture or injury to your arm or leg. There are two methods:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Around your entire arm or leg. This is called a full cast.</li>\n<li>Only on the underside of your arm or leg. This is called a splint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The doctor will determine which cast you will receive.<br>There are two types of cast. The type of cast you receive depends on the fracture and the injury:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>After an accident or surgery, you will usually receive a plaster cast first.</li>\n<li>Once your arm or leg is no longer swollen, you will usually receive a plastic cast. You may also receive a plastic cast after the removal of stitches</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you break your arm, you may need to rest it in a sling.<br>A sling is a strap with a loop that hangs around your neck. Your arm hangs in the loop.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "contentItemTitle": "About the treatment",
      "contentTypeKey": "73fd841a-758a-4e00-8f71-eeeab3cb9cfd",
      "udi": "umb://element/d3669840fd834cbfbe19d0c18ec3b6d2"
    }
  ],
  "settingsData": []
}]]></Value>
    </medicalInfoContentBL>
